WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.048
The landscape at the time of writing.

2
00:00:02.328 --> 00:00:03.544
Provider APIs.

3
00:00:03.824 --> 00:00:07.387
You send text and get vectors back, priced per input token.

4
00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:23.048
Voyage AI (now part of MongoDB): general models voyage-4-large, voyage-4, and voyage-4-lite (quality to cost, in that order), domain models for code, law, and finance, plus multimodal and “contextualized chunk” models.

5
00:00:23.328 --> 00:00:35.253
Defaults to 1,024 dimensions with 256, 512, and 2,048 available, and a 32,000-token context.

6
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:40.483
It also publishes an open-weight model, voyage-4-nano, under Apache 2.

7
00:00:40.763 --> 00:00:41.531
0.

8
00:00:41.811 --> 00:00:57.661
OpenAI: text-embedding-3-small (1,536 dimensions) and text-embedding-3-large (3,072), both with a dimensions parameter to shorten vectors and an 8,192-token input limit.

9
00:00:57.941 --> 00:01:08.245
Google Gemini: gemini-embedding-2 (multimodal: text, images, video, audio, PDF) and the text-only gemini-embedding-001.

10
00:01:08.525 --> 00:01:22.328
Both default to 3,072 dimensions and support 128 to 3,072; the docs recommend 768, 1,536, or 3,072.

11
00:01:22.608 --> 00:01:24.315
Cohere: embed-v5.

12
00:01:24.595 --> 00:01:34.237
0-pro, with over 100 languages, sizes from 256 to 2,048, image inputs, and several compressed output types.

13
00:01:34.517 --> 00:01:35.605
Open models.

14
00:01:35.885 --> 00:01:47.043
You download weights (usually from Hugging Face) and run them with a library such as Sentence Transformers, on a laptop CPU for small jobs or a GPU for large ones.

15
00:01:47.323 --> 00:01:55.536
Families you’ll see often: all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (small and fast, 384 dimensions, English, Apache 2.

16
00:01:55.816 --> 00:02:14.995
0); BGE from the Beijing Academy of AI (Xiao and colleagues, 2023); E5 from Microsoft, including multilingual variants; and Nomic Embed, notable for publishing its training data and code so the model can be reproduced (Nussbaum and colleagues, 2024).

17
00:02:15.275 --> 00:02:20.480
Everything in this list should be rechecked against the providers’ pages before you rely on it.

18
00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.915
The structure of the choice is what lasts.
